E["npc:archmage-ansirem-runeweaver"] = {t="npc",n="Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver",z="alterac",s="At the Violet Citadel, Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver oversees Kirin Tor work as Dalaran is rebuilt. A senior human wizard on the Council of Six, he survived the Scourge's destruction of the city. His willful daughter ran off to Booty Bay to become a pirate.",h="At the Violet Citadel, Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver oversees Kirin Tor work as Dalaran is rebuilt.",sec={{t="A Pillar of the Kirin Tor",b="Ansirem Runeweaver helped defend Dalaran for decades. He holds a seat on the Council of Six, which rules the Kirin Tor. He survived when Arthas Menethil and the Scourge marched on the city and Archimonde was summoned. After Dalaran fell, Ansirem joined the effort to rebuild it. The protective shield came down early, and he now works from the Violet Citadel.",sp=0},{t="Far-Flung Interests",b="Ansirem's ties reach beyond the Alterac Mountains. His willful daughter, Catelyn, ran off to Booty Bay to become a pirate, taking an ancient troll dagger he found while researching in Stranglethorn. Ansirem has dealt with Baron Revilgaz there. He has also studied troll antiquities and keeps diplomatic conduits open across distant realms.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver?",a="Ansirem is an accomplished human wizard and one of the six ruling archmages on the Kirin Tor's Council of Six. After decades defending Dalaran, he now oversees work around the rebuilt city and its arcane perimeter.",al={"who is ansirem","ansirem runeweaver lore","who is the archmage"}},{q="What happened to his daughter?",a="Ansirem's willful daughter, Catelyn, ran off to Booty Bay to become a pirate, where she is known as Catelyn the Blade. She took an ancient troll dagger that Ansirem found while researching in Stranglethorn.",al={"ansirem daughter","catelyn the blade","catelyn runeweaver"}},{q="What is his role in Dalaran?",a="Ansirem is a leading Kirin Tor presence in the Violet Citadel. He coordinates research, magical defense and communication with allies as Dalaran is rebuilt after the Third War's destruction.",al={"why is ansirem in alterac","ansirem dalaran","what is he doing here"}},{q="Did Ansirem fight in the Third War?",a="Yes. Ansirem helped defend Dalaran for decades and survived the Scourge's siege. Arthas guarded Kel'Thuzad's summoning of Archimonde. Ansirem lived through the city's destruction and now helps rebuild it.",al={"ansirem scourge","did ansirem fight arthas"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you can look to Ansirem, a revered member of the Council of Six, for guidance in disciplined arcane study.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you share interests with Ansirem, a Kirin Tor leader based in Lordaeron. Human spellcasters struggle to reclaim their lands from Scourge remnants."},kw={"ansirem","booty bay","catelyn","council of six","dalaran","violet citadel","kirin tor","revilgaz","runeweaver"},rel={"subzone:dalaran","zone:alterac","subzone:booty-bay","npc:baron-revilgaz","topic:third-war","topic:arthas-menethil","topic:alliance"},src={"Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver"}}
E["npc:bath-rah-the-windwatcher"] = {t="npc",n="Bath'rah the Windwatcher",z="alterac",s="Near Chillwind Point, Bath'rah the Windwatcher studies the northern winds in the Alterac Mountains. Far from his tropical homeland, the jungle troll shaman seeks champions strong enough to shape the tempest into weapons.",h="Near Chillwind Point, Bath'rah the Windwatcher studies the northern winds in the Alterac Mountains.",sec={{t="Hermit of the Peaks",b="Bath'rah the Windwatcher keeps to the cold ruins of the Alterac Mountains. Jungle trolls usually dwell among warm forests and coasts, far from these peaks. A seasoned shaman and craftsman, he listens to the wind and communes with nature spirits. He means to bind violent storms into weapons for those strong enough to wield them.",sp=0},{t="Master of Cyclonian",b="Cyclonian is a monstrous wind elemental in the peaks around Bath'rah. He cannot defeat it alone, so he calls on seasoned warriors and shamans to gather exotic elemental essences and summon the creature. When Cyclonian is slain, Bath'rah claims its elemental heart. He uses it to make legendary weapons of raw tempest, renowned across Azeroth.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Bath'rah the Windwatcher?",a="Bath'rah is a jungle troll shaman and weaponcrafter living in seclusion among ruins near Chillwind Point in the Alterac Mountains. He helps seasoned adventurers harness elemental power in weapons.",al={"bathrah identity","who is bathrah","windwatcher lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why is a jungle troll living in Alterac?",a="Bath'rah lives as a hermit near Chillwind Point, studying elemental power and helping capable adventurers forge weapons. The reason he left his homeland is not established.",al={"why is bathrah in alterac","troll in alterac mountains"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Cyclonian?",a="Cyclonian is a massive, violent wind elemental haunting the ruins around Bath'rah's sanctuary. Bath'rah needs its core to forge weapons infused with elemental wind.",al={"who is cyclonian","what does bathrah summon"},it="target"},{q="Why do warriors seek him out?",a="Warriors travel from across the world to Bath'rah because he knows how to forge the Whirlwind weapons. Under his guidance, defeating Cyclonian yields arms infused with howling gales.",al={"bathrah warrior quest","whirlwind axe guy"},it="purpose"},{q="Does Bath'rah only help members of the Horde?",a="Bath'rah lives apart from major faction politics as a solitary hermit. He focuses on elemental craft and helps capable warriors and shamans who respect the spirits and aid his elemental work.",al={"is bathrah hostile","bathrah alliance"},it="side"},{q="What does Bath'rah the Windwatcher want?",a="Bath'rah seeks a worthy champion capable of confronting and defeating Cyclonian, a raging elemental residing near his camp. He covets the creature's heart, hoping to harness its raw primordial energy to forge an extraordinary weapon of immense power.",al={"bath'rah wants","what does bathrah want","bathrah goal"},it="wants",add="4f68ea16"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="Veteran fighters know Bath'rah for guiding them through the trials to forge Whirlwind weapons with the essence of Cyclonian, the wind elemental.",["class:Shaman"]="As a fellow master of the elements, Bath'rah shares a deep spiritual connection with shamans seeking closer communion with the spirits of earth, water, and air."},kw={"alterac","bath'rah","chillwind","cyclonian","elemental","shaman","whirlwind","windwatcher"},rel={"subzone:chillwind-point","zone:alterac","quest:1791","topic:troll"},src={"Bath'rah the Windwatcher"}}
E["npc:lieutenant-haggerdin"] = {t="npc",n="Lieutenant Haggerdin",z="alterac",s="At the Headland gate, Lieutenant Haggerdin gathers recruits for the Stormpike Guard. He watches the entrance to Alterac Valley and honors Alliance champions who prove their valor against the Frostwolf Clan.",h="At the Headland gate, Lieutenant Haggerdin gathers recruits for the Stormpike Guard.",sec={{t="Gatekeeper of the Headland",b="At the snowy Headland above the Hillsbrad Foothills, Lieutenant Haggerdin oversees the Alliance muster for its campaign in Alterac Valley. Dwarven banners mark the massive wooden gate. Recruits and veterans gather under his watch before entering the frigid warzone.",sp=0},{t="Voice of the Stormpike Guard",b="Lieutenant Haggerdin serves the Stormpike Expedition, testing warriors who would represent Ironforge and the Grand Alliance in the valley. In trials such as the Proving Grounds, recruits recover banners and relics. As soldiers rise through the Stormpike Guard, Haggerdin grants official commendations, insignias, and rank recognitions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lieutenant Haggerdin?",a="Lieutenant Haggerdin is a dwarf officer of the Stormpike Guard. He is stationed at the entrance to Alterac Valley on the Headland in the Alterac Mountains, where he oversees Alliance recruitment and awards battlefield honors.",al={"haggerdin","who is haggerdin","lieutenant haggerdin alterac"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Lieutenant Haggerdin?",a="You can find Lieutenant Haggerdin on the Headland in the northern Alterac Mountains, just outside the portal and gates leading into Alterac Valley.",al={"haggerdin location","where is lieutenant haggerdin","alterac valley entrance alliance"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Haggerdin play in the Stormpike Guard?",a="Lieutenant Haggerdin is a field liaison and quartermaster officer for the Stormpike Guard. He administers recruitment trials such as the Proving Grounds and awards higher ranks and insignia as Alliance fighters earn standing with the Guard.",al={"what does haggerdin do","haggerdin quests","stormpike guard officer"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the Alliance fighting in Alterac Valley?",a="The Stormpike Expedition entered Alterac Valley to excavate ancient relics and dwarven history. Their arrival sparked a fierce territorial conflict with the resident Frostwolf orcs and their Horde allies.",al={"why alterac valley","stormpike expedition goal","alterac conflict"},it="conflict"},{q="Can Horde players interact with Lieutenant Haggerdin?",a="No. Lieutenant Haggerdin is an active Alliance officer who attacks Horde champions approaching the Headland gate.",al={"is haggerdin hostile to horde","horde haggerdin","can horde talk to haggerdin"},it="hostile",gp=true},{q="What is the Proving Grounds trial?",a="The Proving Grounds is an introductory trial Lieutenant Haggerdin gives prospective Alliance soldiers. It tests their competence and resolve before they commit fully to the war effort in Alterac Valley.",al={"proving grounds quest","proving grounds alterac","haggerdin proving grounds"}},{q="Whose side is Lieutenant Haggerdin on?",a="Lieutenant Haggerdin is thoroughly loyal to the Alliance, serving specifically within the Stormpike Guard. Operating at the northern edge of the foothills near Alterac Valley, he acts as an officer and muster agent for Alliance forces rallying against the Frostwolf orcs.",al={"haggerdin faction","is haggerdin alliance","haggerdin allegiance"},it="side",add="1d45d886"},{q="What does Lieutenant Haggerdin want?",a="Haggerdin wants capable Alliance champions to bolster the Stormpike Guard's ranks in Alterac Valley. He tests new recruits to ensure they can survive the freezing wilderness, recognizes seasoned veterans with ranks and insignias as their deeds grow, and seeks the downfall of threats like the Winterax troll champion, Korrak.",al={"what does haggerdin want","haggerdin goals","haggerdin purpose"},it="wants",add="5fb68a23"},{q="Why is Lieutenant Haggerdin here in the Alterac foothills?",a="Lieutenant Haggerdin is stationed at the Headland overlooking the gate to Alterac Valley to organize and vet incoming Alliance forces. Because the ongoing clash between the Stormpike Expedition and the Frostwolf Clan demands constant reinforcement, he stands guard at the staging grounds to recruit and honor those willing to fight in the snow.",al={"why is haggerdin here","why is haggerdin in alterac","haggerdin post"},it="why_here",add="96f37aaa"},{q="Who is Lieutenant Haggerdin tied to?",a="Haggerdin is tied directly to the Stormpike Guard, the military arm of Ironforge's Stormpike Expedition led by General Vanndar Stormpike. He serves as an officer linking Alliance recruits arriving through the Alterac Mountains to the regiment fighting deep within Alterac Valley.",al={"haggerdin ties","haggerdin stormpike guard","who does haggerdin serve"},it="ties",add="9b7a183a"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you can find Lieutenant Haggerdin outside Alterac Valley. He offers credentials and official honors earned while fighting the Frostwolf Clan.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may see Ironforge's determination in Lieutenant Haggerdin, a proud Stormpike officer seeking their titan heritage in Alterac's snowy crags.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde champion, you face Lieutenant Haggerdin at the Alliance portal into Alterac Valley. He directs reinforcements sent against the Frostwolf orcs."},kw={"alterac","dwarf","frostwolf","haggerdin","headland","ironforge","lieutenant","proving grounds","stormpike"},rel={"zone:alterac","topic:dwarf","topic:alliance","topic:horde","zone:hillsbrad","topic:alterac-kingdom"},src={"Lieutenant Haggerdin"}}
E["npc:lord-jorach-ravenholdt"] = {t="npc",n="Lord Jorach Ravenholdt",z="alterac",s="At Ravenholdt Manor, Lord Jorach Ravenholdt trains rogues and directs a war against the Syndicate. His estate lies in the Alterac Mountains.",h="At Ravenholdt Manor, Lord Jorach Ravenholdt trains rogues and directs a war against the Syndicate.",sec={{t="Master of the Assassin's League",b="Lord Jorach Ravenholdt commands the Assassin's League from a manor hidden among the crags between Alterac and Hillsbrad. A nobleman of mysterious heritage, he welcomes outlaws, cutpurses, and assassins of any allegiance, provided they show great skill and respect his authority. The league joins master thieves in espionage and killings for hire.\n\nRavenholdt despises the Syndicate, whose members are disgraced Alterac nobles turned outlaws. He sends his followers and visiting rogues to sabotage their camps and plunder their goods.",sp=0},{t="Secrets in the Shadows",b="Lord Jorach Ravenholdt directs operations across Azeroth while the fighting near his manor holds his attention. Rogues who prove loyal take on intricate work across continents to recover guarded artifacts. One effort sought a mysterious Sealed Azure Bag, stolen from Ravenholdt and carried to furbolgs in Azshara.\n\nTo recover it, Archmage Xylem had to decode its secrets, and an Azure Key had to be taken from the Sunken Temple. Ravenholdt also oversees the making of lethal compounds. He sends scouts across the realm to gather venom from ancient horrors.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Lord Jorach Ravenholdt?",a="Lord Jorach Ravenholdt leads the Assassin's League, a covert society of rogues based at Ravenholdt Manor in the mountains above Hillsbrad Foothills. He trains master operatives in stealth and directs assassinations and intelligence gathering.",al={"who is jorach","ravenholdt leader","jorach lore"}},{q="Why does Ravenholdt hate the Syndicate?",a="Ravenholdt's estate lies in land contested by the Syndicate, a network of former Alterac nobles turned outlaws. He opposes their banditry and sends his assassins against their strongholds.",al={"why syndicate enemy","ravenholdt vs syndicate","syndicate rivalry"}},{q="Is Lord Ravenholdt affiliated with the Alliance or Horde?",a="Lord Jorach Ravenholdt's organization is independent. He welcomes rogues from both the Alliance and Horde at his manor, judging them by skill, discipline in stealth, and discretion rather than allegiance.",al={"is ravenholdt alliance","is jorach horde","ravenholdt faction"}},{q="What is inside the Sealed Azure Bag Jorach seeks?",a="What lies inside the Sealed Azure Bag remains a guarded secret. When Lord Jorach Ravenholdt receives the Azure Key and unlocks the enchanted satchel, eerie golden light washes over him. He stares inside in astonishment, then quickly puts it away.",al={"sealed azure bag contents","azure bag mystery","what did jorach get"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can seek Lord Jorach Ravenholdt's patronage. He offers training, poisons, and contracts to rogues who earn his trust."},kw={"alterac","assassin's league","azure key","jorach","ravenholdt","rogue","syndicate","xylem"},rel={"subzone:ravenholdt-manor","topic:ravenholdt","topic:syndicate","zone:alterac","npc:archmage-xylem","subzone:temple-of-atal-hakkar","quest:2300","npc:mathias-shaw"},src={"Lord Jorach Ravenholdt"}}
E["quest:500"] = {t="quest",n="Crushridge Bounty",z="alterac",s="From Southshore, Marshal Redpath warns that Crushridge ogres have settled near Alterac's ruins. He offers a bounty to anyone who hunts them in the Alterac Mountains.",h="From Southshore, Marshal Redpath warns that Crushridge ogres have settled near Alterac's ruins.",sec={{t="Ogres at the Door",b="Marshal Redpath sends you north after reports that Crushridge ogres have dug a mound in the Alterac Mountains near Alterac's ruined city. They have taken the ruins too. Redpath fears they may grow comfortable there, then move down into the foothills and reach Southshore's door. He offers a bounty for hunting them and bringing back the Dirty Knucklebones they carry.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Marshal Redpath want the Crushridge ogres hunted?",a="Redpath fears the Crushridge ogres may grow comfortable in their mound and Alterac's ruins, then move down into the foothills toward Southshore's door.",al={"why kill crushridge ogres","redpath motive","ogre bounty reason"}},{q="Where are the Crushridge ogres?",a="The Crushridge ogres are north in the Alterac Mountains. They have built a mound near Alterac's ruined city, and Redpath's scouts report they hold the ruins too.",al={"ogre location","crushridge ogres where","where to find knucklebones"}},{q="What does Marshal Redpath want brought back?",a="Marshal Redpath wants nine Dirty Knucklebones carried by the Crushridge ogres brought back to him in Southshore.",al={"what do i bring redpath","ogre proof","dirty knucklebones"}}},kw={"alterac","bounty","crushridge","knucklebones","ogres","redpath","southshore"},rel={"quest:504","subzone:southshore","zone:alterac","topic:alterac-kingdom"},m={start="Marshal Redpath",["end"]="Marshal Redpath",level="36",faction="Alliance",id=500},src={"Crushridge Bounty"}}
E["quest:504"] = {t="quest",n="Crushridge Warmongers",z="alterac",s="In the Ruins of Alterac, Crushridge Warmongers face a fiercer hunt. Marshal Redpath of Southshore sends you after them to keep the ogres from Alliance lands.",h="In the Ruins of Alterac, Crushridge Warmongers face a fiercer hunt.",sec={{t="A Harder Lesson",b="Marshal Redpath sends you into the Ruins of Alterac after Crushridge Bounty. He wants you to hunt down many Crushridge Warmongers and strike the Crushridge ogres hard. Redpath believes nothing else will teach the brutes to keep clear of Alliance territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you after the Crushridge Warmongers?",a="Marshal Redpath in Southshore sends you after the Crushridge Warmongers.",al={"who gives crushridge warmongers","questgiver crushridge warmongers","marshal redpath quest"}},{q="Where are the Crushridge Warmongers?",a="They are in the Ruins of Alterac, high in the mountains.",al={"where are crushridge warmongers","warmonger location","crushridge warmongers spot"}},{q="Why does Marshal Redpath want the Warmongers cut down?",a="Redpath believes nothing else will teach the Crushridge ogres to stay away from Alliance lands.",al={"why kill warmongers","purpose of crushridge warmongers","redpath reason ogres"}},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="It follows Crushridge Bounty, Redpath's first call to hunt the Crushridge ogres.",al={"prerequisite for crushridge warmongers","previous quest warmongers","chain before crushridge warmongers"}}},kw={"alterac","crushridge","ogres","redpath","ruins","southshore","warmongers"},rel={"quest:500","subzone:ruins-of-alterac","subzone:southshore","zone:alterac","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:alliance"},m={start="Marshal Redpath",["end"]="Marshal Redpath",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=504},src={"Crushridge Warmongers"}}
E["quest:505"] = {t="quest",n="Syndicate Assassins",z="alterac",s="Southshore’s new magistrate suspects the Syndicate Assassins killed his predecessor. His clues point north of Tarren Mill, where he wants the gang slain.",h="Southshore’s new magistrate suspects the Syndicate Assassins killed his predecessor.",sec={{t="A Magistrate Murdered",b="Magistrate Henry Maleb now holds office in Southshore. The previous magistrate was assassinated, and the killers were never found. Maleb is almost certain the Syndicate hired them.\n\nThieves make up the gang, led by villainous nobles from the fallen kingdom of Alterac. Maleb’s last clues point north of Tarren Mill, which the Horde occupies. He asks you to slay the Syndicate members at the camp there.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Magistrate Henry Maleb want the Syndicate slain?",a="Southshore’s previous magistrate was assassinated, and the killers were never found. Magistrate Henry Maleb is almost certain the Syndicate hired them.",al={"why kill syndicate","syndicate motive","who killed the magistrate"}},{q="Who leads the Syndicate?",a="Villainous nobles from the fallen kingdom of Alterac lead the Syndicate, whose members are thieves.",al={"who runs the syndicate","syndicate leaders","syndicate alterac"}},{q="Where is the Syndicate camp?",a="The Syndicate camp lies north of Tarren Mill, which the Horde occupies. Maleb’s last clues led there.",al={"where are the syndicate footpads","syndicate camp location","where to find syndicate thieves"}}},kw={"alterac","footpad","henry maleb","magistrate","southshore","syndicate","tarren mill","thief"},rel={"npc:magistrate-henry-maleb","subzone:southshore","topic:syndicate","topic:alterac-kingdom","zone:alterac","subzone:tarren-mill"},m={start="Magistrate Henry Maleb",["end"]="Magistrate Henry Maleb",level="33",faction="Alliance",id=505},src={"Syndicate Assassins","In-game quest text: Syndicate Assassins"}}
E["quest:510"] = {t="quest",n="Foreboding Plans",z="alterac",s="The Syndicate's papers call for supplies to reach Southshore soon, where Magistrate Henry Maleb awaits them.",h="The Syndicate's papers call for supplies to reach Southshore soon, where Magistrate Henry Maleb awaits them.",sec={{t="The Supply List",b="The Syndicate papers list food, weapons and clothing. They also call for masks, oil and poison. The supplies are needed soon for an important undertaking against Southshore. Magistrate Henry Maleb is to receive them there.",sp=0},{t="Maleb's Verdict",b="Magistrate Henry Maleb finds the documents troubling. Their words and the Syndicate's past deeds lead him to a grim judgment: the cutthroats have gone to war against the town.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What do the Syndicate documents say?",a="The documents list food, weapons and clothing, along with masks, oil and poison. They say the supplies are needed soon for an important undertaking against Southshore.",al={"what are the foreboding plans","syndicate documents contents","what is in the plans"}},{q="Who should see these plans?",a="Magistrate Henry Maleb in Southshore.",al={"who do i bring the plans to","foreboding plans turn in","where do the plans go"}}},kw={"alterac mountains","foreboding plans","magistrate henry maleb","southshore","syndicate","syndicate documents"},rel={"quest:512","npc:magistrate-henry-maleb","subzone:southshore","topic:syndicate","zone:alterac"},m={start="Syndicate Documents",["end"]="Magistrate Henry Maleb",level="34",faction="Alliance",id=510},src={"Foreboding Plans (quest)"}}
E["quest:511"] = {t="quest",n="Encrypted Letter",z="alterac",s="Among the Syndicate papers, one letter cannot be read. You take it to Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore.",h="Among the Syndicate papers, one letter cannot be read.",sec={{t="A Letter No One Can Read",b="Among the Syndicate documents, one letter is written in a cipher no one can read. You bring it to Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore.",sp=0},{t="What Dibbs Makes of It",b="Loremaster Dibbs has never seen this kind of cipher before. He still has much to learn before he can understand it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does the letter come from?",a="The letter is one of several on a table among the Syndicate documents, and its meaning is unreadable.",al={"letter origin","where find letter","encrypted letter start"}},{q="Who is the letter taken to?",a="You take the letter to Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore.",al={"who reads letter","who can decipher it","dibbs letter"}}},kw={"alterac","encrypted letter","hillsbrad foothills","loremaster dibbs","southshore","syndicate documents"},rel={"quest:514","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","zone:alterac"},m={start="Syndicate Documents",["end"]="Loremaster Dibbs",level="34",faction="Alliance",id=511},src={"Encrypted Letter (Hillsbrad Foothills)"}}
E["quest:512"] = {t="quest",n="Noble Deaths",z="alterac",s="In Southshore, Magistrate Henry Maleb fears the Syndicate means ruin for the town. He sends you north to Strahnbrad's ruins in the Alterac Mountains, where he believes its leaders have their headquarters.",h="In Southshore, Magistrate Henry Maleb fears the Syndicate means ruin for the town.",sec={{t="Hunting the Syndicate's Leaders",b="After Foreboding Plans, Magistrate Henry Maleb wants the Syndicate's leaders struck down before their plans come to pass. Its cutthroats answer to former Alterac nobles, who may hide among ordinary agents. Their signet rings mark them out. Maleb asks you to bring him seven Alterac signet rings in Southshore.\n\nHe believes the Syndicate has made its headquarters among Strahnbrad's ruins, north in the Alterac Mountains.",sp=0},{t="Maleb's Hope",b="Maleb believes the Syndicate could no longer act with decision without its nobility. He thinks it would be reduced to common thugs.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Strahnbrad?",a="Magistrate Henry Maleb in Southshore sends you north to strike at the leaders behind the Syndicate.",al={"quest giver","who gives noble deaths","henry maleb quest"}},{q="Where are the Syndicate nobles located?",a="Maleb believes the Syndicate has made its headquarters among Strahnbrad's ruins, north in the Alterac Mountains.",al={"where to go","strahnbrad location","syndicate nobles location"}},{q="How can you tell the nobles apart from ordinary Syndicate members?",a="The nobles may hide among ordinary Syndicate agents, but their signet rings mark them out.",al={"identifying nobles","who drops rings","how to tell nobles"}},{q="What comes before this in the chain?",a="Foreboding Plans comes before this.",al={"prerequisite quest","previous quest","noble deaths prequest"}}},kw={"alterac mountains","alterac signet ring","henry maleb","noble deaths","southshore","strahnbrad","syndicate"},rel={"quest:510","npc:magistrate-henry-maleb","subzone:strahnbrad","subzone:southshore","topic:syndicate","zone:alterac","topic:alterac-kingdom"},m={start="Magistrate Henry Maleb",["end"]="Magistrate Henry Maleb",level="36",faction="Alliance",id=512},src={"Noble Deaths"}}
E["quest:514"] = {t="quest",n="Letter to Stormpike",z="alterac",s="In Southshore, Loremaster Dibbs entrusts you with an encrypted letter for Ironforge. He hopes Prospector Stormpike can read it.",h="In Southshore, Loremaster Dibbs entrusts you with an encrypted letter for Ironforge.",sec={{t="A Colleague in Ironforge",b="Dibbs sends you to Ironforge to find Prospector Stormpike. He is in the Library, inside the Hall of Explorers. Tell him Dibbs sent you and show him the letter. Dibbs believes no one north of Blackrock Spire can read it better than Stormpike.",sp=0},{t="Stormpike's Welcome",b="When Stormpike learns Dibbs sent you, he asks how the old bookworm is doing. Encryption is his specialty, he says, then begins examining the letter.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Ironforge with the letter?",a="Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore sends you to Ironforge with the letter. He hopes his colleague there can decrypt it.",al={"who gave me this quest","quest giver","who starts letter to stormpike"}},{q="Where is Prospector Stormpike located?",a="Prospector Stormpike is in the Library, inside the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge.",al={"stormpike location","where is stormpike","prospector stormpike library"}},{q="Why does Dibbs believe Stormpike can read the letter?",a="Dibbs believes Stormpike can read the letter if anyone north of Blackrock Spire can.",al={"why stormpike","why send to stormpike","stormpike encryption"}}},kw={"encrypted letter","hall of explorers","ironforge library","letter to stormpike","loremaster dibbs","prospector stormpike","southshore"},rel={"quest:511","quest:525","npc:prospector-stormpike","subzone:library-ironforge","subzone:hall-of-explorers","zone:ironforge","subzone:southshore","zone:alterac"},m={start="Loremaster Dibbs",["end"]="Prospector Stormpike",level="34",faction="Alliance",id=514},src={"Letter to Stormpike"}}
E["quest:522"] = {t="quest",n="Assassin's Contract",z="alterac",s="In Hillsbrad Foothills, a Shadowy Assassin bears a contract naming Magistrate Henry Maleb for death. You are to carry it to Maleb in Southshore, where red wax bears a distinctive signet ring's mark.",h="In Hillsbrad Foothills, a Shadowy Assassin bears a contract naming Magistrate Henry Maleb for death.",sec={{t="A Marked Magistrate",b="A Shadowy Assassin carries a contract in Hillsbrad Foothills. It names Magistrate Henry Maleb for death, and a distinctive signet ring has marked the red wax. Bring the paper to Maleb in Southshore.",sp=0},{t="Maleb's Verdict",b="Magistrate Henry Maleb reads the contract and says it explains Southshore's recent attack. He is certain the Syndicate wants his life, as it wanted the previous magistrate's.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is written in the contract?",a="The contract orders Magistrate Henry Maleb's killing. Red wax seals it, marked by a distinctive signet ring.",al={"what does the contract say","assassins contract details","who is the target"}},{q="Where does this contract originate?",a="A Shadowy Assassin carries the contract in Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"who dropped the contract","where to find contract","shadowy assassin drop"}},{q="To whom should the contract be delivered?",a="Bring the contract to Magistrate Henry Maleb in Southshore. He is the magistrate it names for death.",al={"who do I give the contract to","where to turn in assassins contract","maleb location"}}},kw={"assassin's contract","hillsbrad foothills","magistrate henry maleb","shadowy assassin","signet ring","southshore","syndicate"},rel={"npc:magistrate-henry-maleb","quest:523","subzone:southshore","zone:hillsbrad","topic:syndicate","zone:alterac"},m={start="Assassin's Contract",["end"]="Magistrate Henry Maleb",level="38",faction="Alliance",id=522},src={"Assassin's Contract (quest)"}}
E["quest:523"] = {t="quest",n="Baron's Demise",z="alterac",s="In Southshore, Magistrate Henry Maleb seeks justice for the contract you recovered. Baron Vardus, a cold-hearted nobleman of old Alterac, signed it, and Maleb asks you to bring him his head.",h="In Southshore, Magistrate Henry Maleb seeks justice for the contract you recovered.",sec={{t="Justice for a Contract",b="After Assassin's Contract, Magistrate Henry Maleb tells you Baron Vardus signed the contract. Vardus is a nobleman of old Alterac, known for his cold heart and brutal ways. Maleb is not surprised to find him behind it. Southshore will not let the baron send thugs against the town without answering for it.\n\nMaleb thinks Vardus may be among the Syndicate's haunts, in Strahnbrad's ruins or the valley north of them. He asks you to bring him the baron's head.",sp=0},{t="Maleb's Relief",b="When you bring Baron Vardus's head, Magistrate Henry Maleb thanks you. Knowing the villain has lost his own lets Maleb rest a little easier.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Baron Vardus?",a="Baron Vardus is a nobleman of old Alterac, known for his cold heart and brutal ways. His name is on the contract that marked Magistrate Maleb for death.",al={"baron vardus lore","who is vardus","vardus alterac"}},{q="Why does Magistrate Maleb want Baron Vardus dead?",a="Baron Vardus signed the contract you recovered. Magistrate Maleb will not let him send thugs against Southshore without answering for it.",al={"why kill baron vardus","maleb vardus","reason for baron's demise"}},{q="Where can Baron Vardus be found?",a="Magistrate Maleb thinks Baron Vardus is among the Syndicate's haunts, perhaps in Strahnbrad's ruins or in the valley north of them.",al={"baron vardus location","where is vardus","strahnbrad vardus"}},{q="What comes before this?",a="It follows Assassin's Contract, the contract you recovered bearing Baron Vardus's name.",al={"baron's demise prequest","chain before baron's demise","assassin's contract prerequisite"}}},kw={"alterac mountains","baron vardus","baron's demise","magistrate henry maleb","southshore","strahnbrad","syndicate"},rel={"quest:522","npc:magistrate-henry-maleb","subzone:southshore","subzone:strahnbrad","topic:syndicate","topic:alterac-kingdom","zone:alterac"},m={start="Magistrate Henry Maleb",["end"]="Magistrate Henry Maleb",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=523},src={"Baron's Demise"}}
E["quest:525"] = {t="quest",n="Further Mysteries",z="alterac",s="In the Alterac foothills, a decrypted letter leaves Prospector Stormpike searching for meaning. He sends you to Southshore's magistrate with the message.",h="In the Alterac foothills, a decrypted letter leaves Prospector Stormpike searching for meaning.",sec={{t="A Letter Without Meaning",b="Prospector Stormpike has decrypted the letter you found among thieves in the Alterac foothills. Yet its meaning escapes him, and he wonders why thieves had it at all. Southshore lies nearest to Alterac. If a threat is brewing, its magistrate should hear of it, so you carry the message to Magistrate Henry Maleb.",sp=0},{t="What Maleb Reads",b="Magistrate Henry Maleb studies the letter and judges that no thief or Alterac noble could have written it. Its words point to a darker power behind the Syndicate. Maleb shudders at the thought of what that power might be.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you with the decrypted letter?",a="Prospector Stormpike decrypted the letter but cannot make sense of it. He sends you to Southshore's magistrate because the town lies nearest to Alterac.",al={"who gives further mysteries","further mysteries questgiver","where does further mysteries start"}},{q="Who needs to see the decrypted letter?",a="Magistrate Henry Maleb in Southshore needs to see the decrypted letter. Stormpike says Southshore lies nearest to Alterac, so its magistrate should hear of any brewing threat.",al={"who gets the decrypted letter","further mysteries turn in","where do i take the letter"}},{q="Where did the original encrypted letter come from?",a="You found the original encrypted letter among thieves in the Alterac foothills before taking it to Prospector Stormpike.",al={"origin of the decrypted letter","where was letter found","who had the letter"}}},kw={"alterac","decrypted letter","further mysteries","magistrate henry maleb","prospector stormpike","southshore","syndicate"},rel={"quest:514","quest:537","npc:prospector-stormpike","npc:magistrate-henry-maleb","subzone:southshore","topic:syndicate","zone:alterac"},m={start="Prospector Stormpike",["end"]="Magistrate Henry Maleb",level="34",faction="Alliance",id=525},src={"Further Mysteries"}}
E["quest:535"] = {t="quest",n="Valik",z="alterac",s="In a Syndicate camp, Valik lies dying with an enemy before them. Valik expects you to kill them, but offers answers for a mug of Southshore Stout.",h="In a Syndicate camp, Valik lies dying with an enemy before them.",sec={{t="A Dying Bargain",b="Henchman Valik lies wounded in the Syndicate camp, with you standing before them as an enemy. They expect you to kill them all the same. Yet Valik offers answers to your questions if you bring a mug of Southshore Stout to the camp. They even wonder aloud whether your kind drinks at all.",sp=0},{t="Valik's Last Drink",b="Valik calls the stout the sweetest thing they have ever tasted, though death waits. They hand you something of no use to the dead. Then Valik tells you to get on with it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Valik?",a="Henchman Valik lies injured and dying in the Syndicate camp.",al={"henchman valik","who is valik","valik alterac"}},{q="What does Valik want?",a="Valik wants you to bring a mug of Southshore Stout to the Syndicate camp.",al={"what does valik need","valik drink","valik stout"}},{q="What does Valik promise in return for the stout?",a="Valik promises to share what you seek, though they expect you to kill them afterward.",al={"valik reward lore","what does valik tell you","valik trade"}}},kw={"alterac mountains","henchman valik","southshore stout","syndicate","valik"},rel={"subzone:southshore","topic:syndicate","zone:alterac"},m={start="Henchman Valik",["end"]="Henchman Valik",level="34",faction="Horde",id=535},src={"Valik (quest)"}}
E["quest:537"] = {t="quest",n="Dark Council",z="alterac",s="In Southshore, Magistrate Henry Maleb weighs a letter naming Nagaz and the Argus Wake. He fears they may threaten the land if allied with the Syndicate, and sends you to hunt Nagaz and the Argus Shadow Mages in the Uplands.",h="In Southshore, Magistrate Henry Maleb weighs a letter naming Nagaz and the Argus Wake.",sec={{t="Envoys in the Uplands",b="After Further Mysteries, Maleb tells you the letter came from Nagaz, who belongs to the Argus Wake. He does not know what the Argus Wake is, but fears an alliance with the Syndicate would make them a threat. So he wants Nagaz and the Argus Shadow Mages named in the letter found and killed. Bring him Nagaz’s head.\n\nSearch the Uplands, north of Strahnbrad, where the Syndicate is strongest. Maleb hopes the Argus Wake’s envoys are there.",sp=0},{t="What Maleb Concludes",b="Magistrate Henry Maleb is troubled that a group like the Argus Wake might run the Syndicate. Nagaz, he says, was only another’s servant. The Argus Wake’s reach may run deep across the continent, or even the whole world.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you after Nagaz?",a="Magistrate Henry Maleb in Southshore sends you after Nagaz. He read the letter you brought him.",al={"who gives dark council","dark council questgiver","where to pick up dark council"}},{q="Where are Nagaz and the Argus Shadow Mages located?",a="Maleb tells you to search the Uplands, north of Strahnbrad, where the Syndicate is strongest.",al={"where is nagaz","argus shadow mage location","where are the uplands"}},{q="What is the Argus Wake?",a="Maleb does not know what the Argus Wake is. He knows only that Nagaz belongs to it, and that it must be a threat if allied with the Syndicate.",al={"who are argus wake","what is argus wake","argus wake lore"}},{q="What happens before this?",a="It follows Further Mysteries, when you brought the decrypted letter to Maleb.",al={"prereq for dark council","previous quest","what quest comes before"}}},kw={"argus shadow mage","argus wake","dark council","henry maleb","nagaz","southshore","strahnbrad","syndicate","uplands"},rel={"npc:magistrate-henry-maleb","quest:525","subzone:uplands","subzone:strahnbrad","subzone:southshore","zone:alterac","topic:syndicate"},m={start="Magistrate Henry Maleb",["end"]="Magistrate Henry Maleb",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=537},src={"Dark Council"}}
E["quest:551"] = {t="quest",n="The Ensorcelled Parchment",z="alterac",s="At the top of The Ensorcelled Parchment, Nagaz is the only name clear. A spell hides the rest, so you take it to Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore.",h="At the top of The Ensorcelled Parchment, Nagaz is the only name clear.",sec={{t="A Spell-Veiled Parchment",b="A spell keeps the parchment's writing from being read. Only Nagaz can be made out at the top. You take it to Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore.",sp=0},{t="What Dibbs Makes of It",b="Dibbs asks if the parchment holds more encrypted notes. He wishes he could decipher every odd scrap of writing that drifts out of Alterac. But he admits he lacks the knowledge.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is written on the parchment?",a="A spell hides the writing, except for one word at the top: Nagaz.",al={"what does the ensorcelled parchment say","parchment text","ensorcelled parchment words"}},{q="Who should see the parchment?",a="Show the parchment to Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore. He takes in scraps of lore gathered from the mountains.",al={"loremaster dibbs","who is dibbs","southshore loremaster"}}},kw={"alterac","dibbs","ensorcelled","nagaz","parchment","southshore"},rel={"quest:554","subzone:southshore","zone:alterac","topic:alterac-kingdom"},m={start="Ensorcelled Parchment",["end"]="Loremaster Dibbs",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=551},src={"The Ensorcelled Parchment"}}
E["quest:554"] = {t="quest",n="Stormpike's Deciphering",z="alterac",s="In Ironforge, Loremaster Dibbs sends you to Prospector Stormpike with an ensorcelled parchment.",h="In Ironforge, Loremaster Dibbs sends you to Prospector Stormpike with an ensorcelled parchment.",sec={{t="A Master of Decryption",b="After The Ensorcelled Parchment, Dibbs sends you to Ironforge with the parchment. Prospector Stormpike is studying at the Prospector headquarters. Tell him Dibbs sent you; Dibbs has been bringing Stormpike plenty of business lately.",sp=0},{t="A Matter of Time",b="Prospector Stormpike finds a fine, intricate spell woven over the parchment. He says he can untangle it, but the work will take time, and his time is valuable. He offers to buy the parchment from you.\n\nOnce you agree, Stormpike says he believes no other scholar can translate it. If its contents prove interesting, he promises to send for you.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Prospector Stormpike?",a="Loremaster Dibbs sends you to Prospector Stormpike, whom he calls a master of decryption and deciphering.",al={"who gives the quest","quest giver","loremaster dibbs quest"}},{q="Where can Prospector Stormpike be found?",a="Prospector Stormpike is studying at the Prospector headquarters in Ironforge.",al={"stormpike location","where is stormpike","prospector headquarters"}},{q="Why is the parchment difficult to read?",a="A spell obscures the writing, leaving only the name Nagaz readable at the top.",al={"why ensorcelled parchment","parchment spell","why decipher"}},{q="What comes before this step?",a="The Ensorcelled Parchment comes before this step and brings the enchanted parchment to Dibbs.",al={"previous quest","chain start","prerequisite"}}},kw={"deciphering","dibbs","ensorcelled parchment","ironforge","prospector headquarters","stormpike"},rel={"npc:prospector-stormpike","quest:551","zone:ironforge","zone:alterac"},m={start="Loremaster Dibbs",["end"]="Prospector Stormpike",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=554},src={"Stormpike's Deciphering"}}
E["quest:92432"] = {t="quest",n="An Alarming Request",z="alterac",s="In Southshore, Emissary Jacques warns that Dalaran is in danger. Its ley lines are disrupted, and its constructs have turned erratic and destructive. Archmage Modera sent Jacques to seek outside aid. You are to find her image beside Lordamere Lake, near Dalaran.",h="In Southshore, Emissary Jacques warns that Dalaran is in danger.",sec={{t="Trouble in Dalaran",b="Emissary Jacques brings troubling news from Dalaran. The city's ley lines are disrupted, and its constructs have turned erratic and destructive. No one knows why.\n\nThe high council ordered the matter kept private to spare the order shame. But Jacques says the charade cannot last while the city is being overrun. Jacques was sent by Archmage Modera to seek outside aid. You are to find her image beside Lordamere Lake, near Dalaran.",sp=0},{t="Modera's Welcome",b="Archmage Modera's image greets you with word that Jacques found aid. Though the rules forbid it, pride must not turn allies away in the city's desperate hour. The guards may claim otherwise, but the danger is far from under control.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Emissary Jacques?",a="Emissary Jacques represents Dalaran in Southshore. Archmage Modera sent Jacques to seek outside aid.",al={"emissary jacques","who is jacques","who gives an alarming request"}},{q="What is happening in Dalaran?",a="Dalaran's ley lines are disrupted, and its constructs have turned erratic and destructive. The cause is unknown, and the city is being overrun.",al={"what is wrong in dalaran","dalaran problem","why are constructs attacking dalaran"}},{q="Why is the matter being kept private?",a="The high council ordered the trouble kept private to spare the order shame.",al={"why secrecy dalaran","why hide the constructs","dalaran high council secret"}},{q="Where is the Image of Archmage Modera located?",a="You can find the Image of Archmage Modera beside Lordamere Lake, near Dalaran.",al={"where to find modera","modera location","image of archmage modera"}}},kw={"alterac","constructs","dalaran","jacques","ley lines","lordamere","modera","southshore"},rel={"subzone:dalaran","subzone:southshore","subzone:lordamere-lake","zone:alterac"},m={start="Emissary Jacques",["end"]="Image of Archmage Modera",level="33",faction="Alliance",id=92432},src={"An Alarming Request"},fv=true}
E["quest:92434"] = {t="quest",n="Blood in the Streets",z="alterac",s="Turmoil grips Dalaran after its barrier comes down. Once the patrols are dealt with, Magus Wordeen Voidglare sees a chance for the Horde to enter and learn the mages' secrets. You carry a key from the internment camp to the sewers on the city's northern edge.",h="Turmoil grips Dalaran after its barrier comes down.",sec={{t="A Disagreeable Way In",b="With the patrols dealt with, Magus Wordeen Voidglare says turmoil grips Dalaran since its barrier came down. He urges the Horde to enter and learn the mages' secrets while they can. You carry the key from the internment camp to the sewers on Dalaran's northern edge, by Lordamere Lake. Perhaps the mages left that disagreeable entrance unwarded.",sp=0},{t="What Comes of the Key",b="The Image of Archmage Modera tells you to lower your weapon. She says the key cannot get you past her wards; the mages would not leave such a weakness open now. She says the Horde's interest in her city is no coincidence. She counted on it and has a proposition for you.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you into Dalaran's sewers?",a="Once the patrols are dealt with, Magus Wordeen Voidglare sends you into Dalaran's sewers.",al={"blood in the streets quest giver","who gives blood in the streets","wordeen voidglare quest"}},{q="Where is the entrance into Dalaran located?",a="The sewers lie on Dalaran's northern edge, by Lordamere Lake.",al={"where are dalaran sewers","sewer entrance lordamere lake","how to enter dalaran"}},{q="What key is used to attempt entry?",a="You carry the grimy key from the internment camp.",al={"grimy key dalaran","where did the key come from","internment camp key"}},{q="Why is Dalaran vulnerable right now?",a="Dalaran's barrier has come down, and turmoil grips the city.",al={"why is dalaran barrier down","what happened to dalaran shield"}}},kw={"alterac","blood in the streets","dalaran","grimy key","lordamere lake","modera","sewers","wordeen voidglare"},rel={"quest:545","subzone:dalaran","subzone:sewers","subzone:lordamere-lake","topic:horde","zone:alterac"},m={start="Magus Wordeen Voidglare",["end"]="Image of Archmage Modera",level="34",faction="Horde",id=92434},src={"Blood in the Streets"},fv=true}
E["quest:92459"] = {t="quest",n="Friend of the Kirin Tor",z="alterac",s="In Dalaran, Modera sends you to carry word that the city is calming and its wards may come down.",h="In Dalaran, Modera sends you to carry word that the city is calming and its wards may come down.",sec={{t="The Good Word",b="The Image of Archmage Modera says the council may dislike the subterfuge, but the results are plain. Dalaran is calming, and its wards may now be lowered. She sends you with this good word to Archmage Celindra in the Violet Citadel. For the journey, she gives you an arcane mote.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Archmage Celindra?",a="The Image of Archmage Modera sends you to deliver word that Dalaran is calming.",al={"who gives friend of the kirin tor","friend of the kirin tor quest giver","modera quest"}},{q="Where is Archmage Celindra?",a="Archmage Celindra is in the Violet Citadel, in the City of Dalaran.",al={"where to turn in friend of the kirin tor","who is celindra","archmage celindra location"}},{q="What item do you carry to the Violet Citadel?",a="You carry an arcane mote Modera gives you for Archmage Celindra.",al={"friend of the kirin tor item","what is the arcane mote"}},{q="What is the good word?",a="Dalaran is calming, and its wards may be lowered.",al={"what news does modera send","why lower the wards"}}},kw={"alterac","arcane mote","celindra","dalaran","kirin tor","modera","violet citadel","wards"},rel={"subzone:dalaran","zone:alterac"},m={start="Image of Archmage Modera",["end"]="Archmage Celindra",level="33",faction="Alliance",id=92459},src={"Friend of the Kirin Tor"},fv=true}
E["quest:93680"] = {t="quest",n="Key to the City",z="alterac",s="Wordeen seeks a way into Dalaran, now rebuilt on the Dark Lady’s doorstep.",h="Wordeen seeks a way into Dalaran, now rebuilt on the Dark Lady’s doorstep.",sec={{t="The Rebuilt City",b="In Tarren Mill, Magus Wordeen Voidglare wants to learn more about the Kirin Tor. Their city, Dalaran, fell to the demonic Burning Legion in a single stroke from the arch demon Archimonde. The surviving mages became dispossessed vagabonds. Now they have rebuilt Dalaran on the Dark Lady’s very doorstep.\n\nWordeen sends you to search their camps. He hopes you will find an ancient tome, a secret relic, or something else that can get the Horde into the city unnoticed. What you bring back is a grimy Dalaran sewer key.",sp=0},{t="Wordeen's Answer",b="Wordeen sees the sewer key and gives thanks that someone else will use it. There is work to do before it is safe to use.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the request for Key to the City?",a="Magus Wordeen Voidglare in Tarren Mill asks you to help.",al={"who gives key to the city","key to the city questgiver","where do i start key to the city"}},{q="Why is the Horde interested in Dalaran?",a="The Kirin Tor have rebuilt Dalaran on the Dark Lady’s doorstep after Archimonde destroyed their city. Wordeen wants to learn more about them and find a way for the Horde to enter unnoticed.",al={"why dalaran","why watch dalaran","what are the mages doing"}},{q="What item are you sent to find?",a="You are sent to search the Kirin Tor camps for a grimy Dalaran sewer key.",al={"what do i get for wordeen","what is the key","key to the city item"}}},kw={"archimonde","burning legion","dalaran","grimy key","kirin tor","sewer key","tarren mill","wordeen voidglare"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:dalaran","quest:545","zone:alterac","topic:burning-legion"},m={start="Magus Wordeen Voidglare",level="33",faction="Horde",id=93680},src={"Key to the City (Forever)"},fv=true}
E["quest:97287"] = {t="quest",n="Shrewd Negotiations",z="alterac",s="After your infiltration of the mages' city, Magus Wordeen Voidglare sends you to Dalaran. Carry the arcane mote to Archmage Celindra; Wordeen believes the Kirin Tor will give anything to recover it.",h="After your infiltration of the mages' city, Magus Wordeen Voidglare sends you to Dalaran.",sec={{t="Time to Negotiate",b="Magus Wordeen Voidglare says no order on Azeroth matches the Kirin Tor in arcane knowledge. Even his brilliant work pales beside their ancient wisdom. He believes the Horde should gain access to their exclusive order. So he sends you to Archmage Celindra in Dalaran with the mote you acquired. Wordeen believes the Kirin Tor will give anything to get it back.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to negotiate with Dalaran?",a="Magus Wordeen Voidglare sends you to Dalaran after your infiltration of the city.",al={"who gives shrewd negotiations","wordeen voidglare","quest giver shrewd negotiations"}},{q="Who are you sent to speak with?",a="You are sent to speak with Archmage Celindra in Dalaran.",al={"who do i talk to","celindra location","where is celindra"}},{q="What leverage do you carry?",a="You carry the arcane mote you acquired. Wordeen believes the Kirin Tor will give anything to recover it.",al={"what is the mote","bargaining chip","arcane mote"}},{q="Why does Wordeen Voidglare want to deal with Dalaran?",a="Wordeen says no place on Azeroth rivals the Kirin Tor in arcane knowledge. He believes the Horde should gain access to their exclusive order.",al={"why negotiate with kirin tor","wordeen motive","why dalaran"}}},kw={"alterac mountains","arcane mote","archmage celindra","dalaran","kirin tor","shrewd negotiations","wordeen voidglare"},rel={"subzone:dalaran","zone:alterac"},m={start="Magus Wordeen Voidglare",["end"]="Archmage Celindra",level="33",faction="Horde",id=97287},src={"Shrewd Negotiations"},fv=true}
E["subzone:alterac-mountains"] = {t="subzone",n="Alterac Mountains",z="alterac",s="In the Alterac Mountains, ruined settlements and bandits claim the slopes above Hillsbrad’s pastures. Once the heart of a proud human kingdom, the highlands now offer travelers little safety.",h="In the Alterac Mountains, ruined settlements and bandits claim the slopes above Hillsbrad’s pastures.",sec={{t="A Fallen Realm",b="The Alterac highlands once held a sovereign human nation, one of seven kingdoms born from ancient Arathor. During the Second War, King Aiden Perenolde secretly made a pact with the Old Horde. He let orcish forces cross the peaks in return for his kingdom’s safety. The Alliance of Lordaeron uncovered the betrayal and deposed him. Martial law and territorial disputes left the region divided.",sp=0},{t="Wilderness and Bandits",b="The Third War’s devastation left the mountains lawless. Disinherited nobles formed the Syndicate, which works from Strahnbrad’s ruins and plots to reclaim its lost dominion through sabotage and assassination. Crushridge ogres hold the shattered capital. Gnolls roam the slopes, and the magical ruins around Dalaran lie shattered. Alterac’s passes remain among Lordaeron’s most perilous paths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What kingdom used to rule these mountains?",a="The human kingdom of Alterac ruled these mountains for generations after the Empire of Arathor splintered. Its capital stood among the highest peaks, commanding roads between Lordaeron, Dalaran, and the Arathi highlands. Alterac fell during the Second War.",al={"who owned alterac","what was alterac","alterac kingdom lore"},it="history"},{q="Why is Alterac in ruins?",a="During the Second War, King Aiden Perenolde betrayed the Alliance of Lordaeron by helping the Horde. When his treason came to light, Alliance armies crushed Alterac’s forces and deposed the crown. Without a legitimate ruler, and after the Third War’s devastation, the nation collapsed into rubble.",al={"what happened to alterac","who destroyed alterac","ruins of alterac backstory"},it="ruin"},{q="Who are the Syndicate lurking in the hills?",a="The Syndicate is an outlaw faction of former Alteraci nobles and their retainers. Led by Aliden Perenolde, its members employ brigands, assassins, and rogue mercenaries to destabilize the region. They hope to restore their kingdom through violence.",al={"who is the syndicate","what is the syndicate","why are there bandits in alterac"},it="people"},{q="What threats wander the snowy peaks?",a="Travelers on the slopes face brutal Crushridge ogres, packs of Highland gnolls, scavenging kobolds, and Syndicate brigands who patrol the passes.",al={"what lives in alterac","alterac monsters","threats in alterac"},it="danger"},{q="What are the Alterac Mountains?",a="The Alterac Mountains are a rugged, snow-capped range rising in central Lordaeron just north of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Once the sovereign territory of the human kingdom of Alterac, these heights held fortified cities, mountain keeps, and remote valleys. Today, the nation is broken and its towns lie shattered in the snow, leaving the freezing peaks a battleground for lingering outcasts, warring clans, and predatory monsters.",al={"what is alterac mountains","alterac mountains lore","alterac region overview"},it="place",add="e4635e9a"},{q="Who rules the Alterac Mountains today?",a="No legitimate government holds the Alterac Mountains. The kingdom collapsed after its treason in the Second War, and whatever order remained vanished during the Scourge's onslaught. Today, the Syndicate—dispossessed human nobles and outlaws led by the Perenolde bloodline—claims ancestral rights to the ruins. However, they violently contend with brutish Crushridge ogres, wandering undead, and entrenched Frostwolf orcs hidden in the high valleys.",al={"who controls alterac","who lives in alterac mountains","alterac leadership"},it="residents",add="858b3945"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the Alterac Mountains recall Perenolde’s treachery, which nearly doomed humanity during the Second War.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you find the mountain passes thick with Syndicate agents and hired cutthroats. These hills test your survival and skill at counter-espionage."},kw={"alterac","crushridge","hillsbrad","mountains","perenolde","strahnbrad","syndicate"},rel={"zone:hillsbrad","zone:alterac","subzone:ruins-of-alterac","subzone:strahnbrad","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:syndicate","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","subzone:dalaran"},src={"Alterac Mountains"}}
E["subzone:alterac-mountains-classic"] = {t="subzone",n="Alterac Mountains (Classic)",z="alterac",s="In the Alterac Mountains, ogres, outlaws, and armies fight over the highlands. North of Hillsbrad Foothills, rain darkens the slopes beneath snowbound peaks. Once home to Alterac and Dalaran, the region now lies largely in ruins.",h="In the Alterac Mountains, ogres, outlaws, and armies fight over the highlands.",sec={{t="A Shattered Highland",b="Rain falls over the Alterac Mountains, where pine forests climb toward snow at the highest reaches. Three human powers once held these heights: the mountain kingdom of Alterac, the magocracy of Dalaran, and the fortified town of Strahnbrad. Betrayal and war brought them low. Crushridge ogres occupy Alterac's ruined capital, and outlaws hold Strahnbrad. Among Dalaran's shattered remains, surviving wizards labor to restore their ruined sanctuary.",sp=0},{t="Bandits, Beasts, and War",b="Mountain lions and yeti stalk the frostbitten ridges, while desperate factions fight for the uplands. The Syndicate are dispossessed human nobles turned brigands. From old estates and foothill camps, they strike with blades and ambushes. They clash without end with the advancing ogres.\n\nDeep passes into the high crags hold staging camps for the bloody war between the Stormpike Expedition and the Frostwolf Clan. Both fight over the hidden reaches of Alterac Valley.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to the kingdom of Alterac?",a="Alterac fell into disgrace during the Second War, when King Aiden Perenolde betrayed the Grand Alliance and aided the Horde. After the war, the kingdom was dismantled. Without leadership, its cities crumbled. Strahnbrad fell to ruin, and Crushridge ogres overran the capital.",al={"why is alterac in ruins","who ruled alterac","fall of alterac"}},{q="Who are the Syndicate bandits in the mountains?",a="The Syndicate is an outlaw organization made mostly of former Alterac nobles and their retainers. After losing their land, status, and wealth in Alterac's betrayal, they turned to espionage, assassination, and highway robbery. They seek to reclaim lands they believe are rightfully theirs.",al={"who is the syndicate","why are there rogues in alterac","alterac bandits"}},{q="What is the massive purple dome on the lake shore?",a="No dome stands over Dalaran today. After the demon lord Archimonde razed the city during the Third War, the surviving Kirin Tor mages raised a violet shield over the ruins. They removed it early in reconstruction and now rebuild their devastated towers in the open.",al={"purple bubble in alterac","what is dalaran bubble","magical shield dalaran"}},{q="How do you reach Alterac Mountains?",a="Most travelers enter the Alterac Mountains on foot from Hillsbrad Foothills, taking northern roads from Tarren Mill or from north of Southshore. Daring swimmers can also cross southeast over Lordamere Lake from the shores of Silverpine Forest or the outskirts of the Undercity.",al={"how to get to alterac","alterac entrance","path to alterac"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Ravenholdt Manor lies in a secluded mountain valley on Alterac's border. It is the historic headquarters of the thieves' and assassins' guild, led by Lord Jorach Ravenholdt.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance keeps a forward outpost in these frozen hills under Lieutenant Haggerdin. There, it recruits stalwart fighters to reinforce the dwarven Stormpike Guard in Alterac Valley."},kw={"alterac mountains","alterac valley","crushridge ogres","dalaran","lordamere","ruins of alterac","strahnbrad","syndicate","uplands"},rel={"zone:alterac","subzone:ruins-of-alterac","subzone:strahnbrad","subzone:dalaran","subzone:ravenholdt-manor","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:syndicate","zone:hillsbrad"},src={"Alterac Mountains (Classic)"}}
E["subzone:dalaran"] = {t="subzone",n="Dalaran",z="alterac",s="On Lordamere Lake, Dalaran's surviving magi are rebuilding their shattered city. Once the shining capital of the Kirin Tor, it fell to the Scourge and Archimonde during the Third War. Its protective violet shield has been removed.",h="On Lordamere Lake, Dalaran's surviving magi are rebuilding their shattered city.",sec={{t="Fall of the Magocracy",b="Dalaran began as a sanctuary for arcane study, founded by sorcerers of the Arathorian Empire after the ancient Troll Wars. For centuries, it was humanity's foremost center of magic. The Council of Six led the Kirin Tor, keeping vast archives and powerful artifacts in the Violet Citadel.\n\nThat age ended during the Third War. The traitor prince Arthas led the Scourge through the city gates to seize the Book of Medivh. Soon after, the demon lord Archimonde crushed Dalaran's soaring spires into rubble.",sp=0},{t="Rebuilding the Magocracy",b="After the Legion's defeat, the Kirin Tor's surviving wizards returned to their devastated homeland. They would not yield their ancestral ground to the Scourge or scavengers, and raised a shimmering violet barrier over the city's heart. The shield has since been removed, while rebuilding continues. The magi are restoring their fallen sanctuary, and Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver can be found in the Violet Citadel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What became of Dalaran's protective shield?",a="After Dalaran's destruction in the Third War, the Kirin Tor raised a magical shield over the city. The shield has since been removed, and rebuilding continues.",al={"purple bubble","purple shield alterac","what is the dome","dalaran dome"}},{q="Can players enter Dalaran?",a="Yes. Reconstruction is underway, and Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver resides in the Violet Citadel. The Kirin Tor sides with the Alliance, and the Horde is Hated by them and attacked on sight in the city. Horde groups can still enter the City of Dalaran dungeon.",al={"can i get inside dalaran","how to enter dalaran","get past dalaran shield"}},{q="Who destroyed Dalaran?",a="Prince Arthas and his Scourge army attacked Dalaran and stole the Book of Medivh from its vaults. Soon after, the demon lord Archimonde used dark sorcery to pulverize the city into ruins.",al={"how did dalaran fall","who blew up dalaran","why is dalaran in ruins"}},{q="Who rules Dalaran?",a="The Kirin Tor governs Dalaran through its ruling assembly, the Council of Six.",al={"who runs dalaran","dalaran leadership","who leads kirin tor"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you look to Dalaran as the historic cradle of human and high elven wizardry. Its legendary spires are still being rebuilt, a solemn reminder of the losses mages suffered in the Third War.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can trace Dalaran's place in your history to its role as one of the seven founding kingdoms of the original Alliance of Lordaeron. The Kirin Tor is rebuilding its devastated capital."},kw={"alterac","archimonde","council of six","dalaran","dome","kirin tor","lordamere","shield","violet citadel"},rel={"zone:alterac","subzone:lordamere-lake","topic:third-war","topic:scourge","topic:burning-legion","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Dalaran"}}
E["subzone:dandred-s-fold"] = {t="subzone",n="Dandred's Fold",z="alterac",s="Syndicate outlaws hold Dandred's Fold on Lordamere Lake's northwestern shore. The farmstead and manor shelter Lord Aliden Perenolde and his co-conspirators. The Horde and Alliance watch the estate for different reasons.",h="Syndicate outlaws hold Dandred's Fold on Lordamere Lake's northwestern shore.",sec={{t="A Noble Safe Haven Fallen to Outlaws",b="On the western edge of the Uplands, Dandred's Fold stands beside Lordamere Lake, apart from the surrounding country. The estate was once tranquil and may have belonged to an Alteraci noble named Dandred. After Alterac fell, the Syndicate turned it into a fortified refuge. Its assassins and enforcers patrol the grounds. They keep Southshore authorities and the Forsaken across the lake from the fallen nobility sheltered within.",sp=0},{t="A Nexus of Intrigues",b="Lord Aliden Perenolde leads the Syndicate and makes Dandred's Fold his base. His mistress, Elysa, is with him there. Nagaz has also made his place at the manor. A rogue Shadow Council orc of the Argus Wake, he brokers dark pacts with the human brigands. This alliance has drawn the attention of Southshore's magistrates and Horde champions.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who controls Dandred's Fold?",a="The Syndicate occupies Dandred's Fold. It is an aristocratic criminal network led by Alterac's deposed nobles, and its assassins and enforcers guard the estate under Lord Aliden Perenolde.",al={"who is at dandreds fold","who lives at dandred's fold","dandreds fold mobs"},it="residents"},{q="Why does the Horde care about this estate?",a="The Horde targets the manor to strike down Lord Aliden Perenolde and retrieve a stolen keepsake. It is the heirloom necklace of Taretha Foxton, Thrall's childhood savior and confidante.",al={"horde dandreds fold","why horde go to dandreds fold"},sp=1,it="conflict",bt={"q533.6"}},{q="Why does the Alliance send adventurers here?",a="Magistrate Henry Maleb of Southshore sends Alliance agents to eliminate Nagaz. He is a dangerous member of the Argus Wake cult who colludes with the Syndicate outlaws.",al={"alliance dandreds fold","magistrate maleb quest dandreds fold"}},{q="Who was Dandred?",a="No confirmed account identifies Dandred. The estate bears his name, but its original owner is unknown.",al={"who is dandred","dandred lore"},it="name"},{q="What is Dandred's Fold?",a="Dandred's Fold is a secluded farm and manor perched on the western Uplands of the Alterac Mountains, bordering the misty shores of Lordamere Lake. Once a peaceful noble estate, it now serves as a fortified haven and operational base for the Syndicate.",al={"what is dandreds fold","dandreds fold alterac","about dandreds fold"},it="place",add="e469c160"},{q="What happened at Dandred's Fold?",a="Following the collapse of the Kingdom of Alterac, this lakeside farm fell into the hands of the Syndicate. Lord Aliden Perenolde turned the isolated manor into a personal stronghold and retreat, forging dangerous ties with shadowy organizations like the Argus Wake.",al={"dandreds fold history","what happened to dandreds fold"},it="history",add="b8b5cedb"},{q="Is Dandred's Fold dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous for lone travelers. The grounds are guarded by skilled Syndicate enforcers, stealthy cutthroats, and covert agents of the Argus Wake, all fiercely loyal to Lord Aliden Perenolde and hostile to outside intruders.",al={"is dandreds fold dangerous","dandred fold danger","who is at dandreds fold"},it="danger",add="fc1f4fab"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, Dandred's Fold is personal. Warchief Thrall seeks the return of Taretha Foxton's necklace.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance cannot tolerate an alliance between human outlaws and the demonic Argus Wake. Magistrate Henry Maleb orders strikes against the estate."},kw={"aliden perenolde","argus wake","dandred's fold","dandreds fold","elysa","lordamere lake","nagaz","syndicate","uplands"},rel={"topic:syndicate","zone:alterac","npc:magistrate-henry-maleb","subzone:uplands","subzone:lordamere-lake","subzone:misty-shore","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:alliance"},src={"Dandred's Fold"}}
E["subzone:lordamere-internment-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Lordamere Internment Camp",z="alterac",s="Surviving Dalaran magi and guards hold Lordamere Internment Camp above Dalaran. The old prison also shelters Forsaken defectors.",h="Surviving Dalaran magi and guards hold Lordamere Internment Camp above Dalaran.",sec={{t="From Prison to Research Outpost",b="Lordamere Internment Camp now serves Dalaran’s remnants as a research outpost. After the Second War, the Alliance built camps across the northern kingdoms to hold the defeated orcish Horde. Lordamere was the only camp in the Alterac Mountains, and Dalaran oversaw it. The orcs have long since been freed or fled. Warden Belamoore leads the camp, where Dalaran’s survivors study dangerous magical relics.",sp=0},{t="Forsaken Defectors",b="Four Forsaken renegades, including Kegan Darkmar, fled to Lordamere with Bloodstone artifacts stolen from the Undercity. They traded the relics to Warden Belamoore for sanctuary behind Dalaran’s lines. The magi accepted them for arcane study. In Tarren Mill, executors send loyal Horde operatives to hunt the defectors and recover the stolen Bloodstones before Dalaran unlocks their power.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What was this camp originally built for?",a="After the Second War, the Alliance built the camp to imprison orcs who had grown lethargic after losing their demonic bloodlust. Dalaran manned its watchtowers and oversaw it because it stood so close to the magi’s city.",al={"internment camp history","why is there a camp here","what is this place"}},{q="Who controls the camp right now?",a="Warden Belamoore and a detachment of Dalaran guards and magi hold the camp. Though Dalaran suffered heavy damage, its survivors continue their research from the fortified hilltop.",al={"who lives here","who runs the camp","who is warden belamoore"}},{q="Why are there undead Forsaken inside the camp?",a="Kegan Darkmar leads the deserters from the Undercity. They betrayed Queen Sylvanas and stole sacred Bloodstone artifacts, then traded the relics to Warden Belamoore for protection from Forsaken retribution.",al={"undead here","kegan darkmar","forsaken deserters"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The deserters at Lordamere have betrayed the Dark Lady. Hunting Kegan Darkmar and recovering the Bloodstones is vital to keeping Forsaken secrets from human hands.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs, Lordamere recalls the years after the Second War, when thousands of their kin withered in captivity before Thrall rallied their people."},kw={"alterac","belamoore","bloodstone","dalaran","internment","kegan darkmar","lordamere","orcs"},rel={"zone:alterac","subzone:dalaran","topic:second-war","topic:forsaken","topic:horde"},src={"Lordamere Internment Camp"}}
E["subzone:misty-shore"] = {t="subzone",n="Misty Shore",z="alterac",s="Along Lordamere Lake's eastern bank, Misty Shore lies between Dandred's Fold and Dalaran. Fog softens the view across the water, where the Dawning Isles and Fenris Keep rise in the distance.",h="Along Lordamere Lake's eastern bank, Misty Shore lies between Dandred's Fold and Dalaran.",sec={{t="A Fog-Shrouded Waterline",b="Misty Shore is a lakeside stretch of the Alterac Mountains, running up to Dalaran's perimeter. Damp air drifts off the water, often hiding snapping turtles along the shore. Zealous fanatics sometimes wander down from nearby strongholds.",sp=0},{t="Watching the Lake",b="Across Lordamere Lake, the Dawning Isles and Fenris Keep rise through the fog. Dalaran lies nearby, with Scarlet-controlled pockets close at hand. Travelers keep a low profile along the bank to avoid unwanted attention.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Misty Shore located?",a="Misty Shore follows the eastern shore of Lordamere Lake in the Alterac Mountains, between Dandred's Fold and Dalaran's perimeter.",al={"misty shore location","where is misty shore","misty shore map"},it="place"},{q="What can be seen across the water from here?",a="From the shore you can make out the Dawning Isles and Fenris Keep across Lordamere Lake, half hidden in fog.",al={"what is across the water","misty shore view","lake view"}},{q="What threats are typically found along the shore?",a="Snapping turtles inhabit the shoreline. Travelers may also encounter Scarlet Crusade zealots or scouts from nearby farmsteads and ruins.",al={"misty shore danger","enemies at misty shore","creatures on misty shore"},it="threat"},{q="What is Misty Shore?",a="Misty Shore is a quiet, fog-shrouded stretch of shoreline bordering the eastern shore of Lordamere Lake in the Alterac Mountains. It extends roughly between Dandred's Fold and the perimeter of Dalaran, offering a clear view across the lake toward the Dawning Isles and the distant towers of Fenris Keep.",al={"what is misty shore","about misty shore","misty shore overview"},it="place",add="140433c1"},{q="Is Misty Shore dangerous?",a="While it appears placid at first glance, the shore is far from safe. The waters and banks teem with aggressive snapjaw turtles, and travelers must watch for hostile humans aligned with the Scarlet Crusade who patrol nearby, attacking anyone they perceive as tainted or trespassers.",al={"how dangerous is misty shore","misty shore dangers","is misty shore safe"},it="danger",add="fbe1f33b"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Snapping turtles along Lordamere Lake provide meat for cooks traveling through Alterac.",["faction:Horde"]="The misty bank offers a sheltered approach between Forsaken-held lands near Tarren Mill and the northern lakeshore, away from open patrols."},kw={"alterac mountains","dandred's fold","dawning isles","fenris keep","lordamere lake","misty shore","turtles"},rel={"subzone:lordamere-lake","zone:alterac","subzone:dandred-s-fold","subzone:fenris-isle","subzone:fenris-keep","subzone:dawning-isles","topic:scarlet-crusade"},src={"Misty Shore"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-alterac"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Alterac",z="alterac",s="Snow lies over the Ruins of Alterac, where Crushridge ogres now hold the old mountain capital. After King Aiden Perenolde betrayed the Alliance in the Second War, Alterac was cast out and placed under martial law.",h="Snow lies over the Ruins of Alterac, where Crushridge ogres now hold the old mountain capital.",sec={{t="A Kingdom's Betrayal",b="Alterac once ruled as an independent human realm, carved from the old Arathor empire and set high on mountain trade routes. During the Second War, King Aiden Perenolde feared the invading Old Horde would destroy his kingdom, so he secretly made a pact with the orcs. After the fighting at Caer Darrow, the betrayal came to light. The Alliance of Lordaeron struck swiftly.\n\nKing Terenas Menethil II placed the city under martial law and deposed Perenolde. The people fled or turned to outlawry, and the grand fortifications, church, and palace fell into disrepair.",sp=0},{t="The Ogre Occupation",b="Surviving Alteraci nobles and rogue soldiers formed the Syndicate. They waged guerrilla campaigns from towns like Strahnbrad, but lost their ancestral capital. Today, Crushridge ogres under Mug'thol dwell among broken ramparts, palace halls, and wrecked ballistae. Neither the Syndicate nor Southshore's human defenders have reclaimed the fallen city.\n\nIts crumbling towers and abandoned vaults remain dangerous ground for treasure hunters and scavengers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was Alterac destroyed?",a="During the Second War, King Aiden Perenolde allied with the invading Orcish Horde, hoping to spare his kingdom. The Alliance of Lordaeron uncovered his treason and struck swiftly. Its forces invaded Alterac City, dismantled its defenses, and placed the kingdom under martial law.",al={"why is alterac in ruins","what happened to alterac city","fall of alterac"},it="ruin"},{q="Who lives in the ruins now?",a="The Crushridge ogres, led by Mug'thol, have overtaken the palace, walls, and snowed-in courtyards. Bro'kin, an enterprising goblin alchemy vendor, sits quietly atop the northern ramparts.",al={"who controls alterac ruins","alterac ogres","who is in alterac"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Syndicate's connection to this place?",a="The Syndicate is made up largely of former Alteraci aristocracy and soldiers who lost their lands when the kingdom was dissolved. They bitterly long to reclaim Alterac, but the Crushridge ogres drove them from the capital. Now they operate from outposts like Strahnbrad.",al={"does the syndicate live here","syndicate alterac connection"},it="ties"},{q="Why do Alliance adventurers come here?",a="Alliance soldiers from Southshore offer bounties on the hostile Crushridge ogres, who raid the roads. Nobles in the south, including Count Remington Ridgewell, also send agents into the ruins to recover lost family heirlooms like the Perenolde Tiara.",al={"alliance quests alterac ruins","crushridge bounty"},it="motive"},{q="Why is the Horde interested in these ruins?",a="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken take an active interest in artifacts scattered across the fallen human kingdom. They send champions into the ogre-infested stronghold to secure relics of power such as the Crown of Will.",al={"horde quests alterac ruins","sylvanas alterac"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Ruins of Alterac?",a="These snowbound stone walls and broken parapets are all that remain of Alterac City, once the proud mountain capital of the human Kingdom of Alterac. Founded thousands of years ago following the expansion of Arathor, the city guarded the vital trade routes winding through the mountains until its king's treachery brought about its downfall during the Second War.",al={"what is ruins of alterac","ruins of alterac overview","alterac city"},it="place",add="46d22466"},{q="What happened to Alterac City during the Second War?",a="During the Second War, King Aiden Perenolde struck a clandestine pact with the invading Orcish Horde to spare his realm. When the Alliance of Lordaeron discovered Alterac's treason, Alliance forces marched upon the mountain kingdom, razing the capital and placing the remnants under martial law. Deposed and disgraced, Perenolde was imprisoned, leaving the kingdom shattered and abandoned.",al={"alterac city history","what happened at alterac","fall of alterac"},it="history",add="967fd086"},{q="How dangerous are the Ruins of Alterac?",a="Extremely dangerous for the unprepared. The Crushridge ogres have made the snow-covered streets and dilapidated halls their home, fiercely defending their territory against any who trespass. Compounding the peril, the ruins occasionally draw the attention of the ruthless Syndicate and wandering undead, leaving the mountain passes treacherous and fraught with ambush.",al={"is ruins of alterac dangerous","ruins of alterac threats","alterac city dangers"},it="danger",add="fd0078c8"},{q="Why is this place called the Ruins of Alterac?",a="The site takes its name from the ancient human kingdom and city of Alterac that once stood here. Following the kingdom's dissolution and the physical devastation wrought during the Second War, nothing survived of the grand capital except cracked masonry, shattered gates, and crumbling towers, reducing the once-mighty seat of power to a mere ruined landmark.",al={"why called ruins of alterac","ruins of alterac name origin"},it="name",add="fbcb07c6"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of the Alliance, these ruins recall human weakness and treason during the Second War. Perenolde's cowardice broke the brotherhood of the Seven Kingdoms.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you hear echoes of the Old Horde's former alliances in this fallen city. The Forsaken can scavenge magical relics while the Crushridge ogres are distracted."},kw={"alterac city","bro'kin","crushridge","mug'thol","perenolde","ruins of alterac","strahnbrad","syndicate"},rel={"topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:syndicate","zone:alterac","subzone:strahnbrad","quest:543","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","topic:terenas-menethil-ii","topic:second-war"},src={"Ruins of Alterac"}}
E["subzone:uplands"] = {t="subzone",n="Uplands",z="alterac",s="In the northeastern Alterac Mountains, the Syndicate holds the Uplands and its camps. These hills once fed Alterac's mountain fortresses, but now shelter the band's strongest base.",h="In the northeastern Alterac Mountains, the Syndicate holds the Uplands and its camps.",sec={{t="Breadbasket to Bandit Stronghold",b="Before the Second War broke Alterac apart, grain and livestock from the Uplands fed its mountain fortresses. When the kingdom fell into ruin, honest folk left their farms behind. Dispossessed nobles and cutthroats formed the Syndicate, set on taking back what they believed was stolen from them by force. Its camps, patrols, and outposts now fill the hills. Dandred's Fold lies along the western borders.",sp=0},{t="A Seat of Shadows",b="The Syndicate keeps its strongest forces in the Uplands. There, high-ranking conspirators oversee its operations, including Baron Vardus, who is aligned with the shadowy leaders guiding Alterac's remaining nobility. From these hills they direct brigands, raid neighboring valleys, and resist both the Alliance and Horde. Travelers on the northeastern ridges meet entrenched highwaymen who claim the range as their sovereign soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Uplands originally used for?",a="The Uplands once fed Alterac's mountain fortresses with grain and livestock. It was the kingdom's main agricultural region before war and betrayal brought its downfall.",al={"uplands history","what used to be here","uplands purpose"},it="history"},{q="Who controls the Uplands now?",a="The Syndicate controls the Uplands. Alterac's former nobles and their bandit network have built several camps here, where their forces are strongest.",al={"who lives in uplands","who holds the uplands","uplands factions"},it="residents"},{q="Where is the Uplands located?",a="The Uplands lies in the northeastern highlands of the Alterac Mountains. Dandred's Fold sits along its western edge.",al={"uplands location","where is uplands","how to find uplands"},it="place"},{q="Who is Baron Vardus?",a="Baron Vardus is an influential Syndicate noble who oversees operations in the Uplands. He directs bandits and conspirators seeking to reclaim Alterac.",al={"baron vardus lore","who is vardus","uplands baron"}},{q="Why is the Uplands ruined and abandoned?",a="The Uplands once flourished as the breadbasket of the kingdom of Alterac, filled with fertile fields and homesteads. When the kingdom collapsed following its betrayal during the Second War, its heartland was shattered. Without the kingdom's protection, the agricultural heart of the region withered and was overrun by criminals, leaving ruins like Dandred's Fold in its wake.",al={"why is uplands ruined","what happened to uplands farms","why is uplands abandoned"},it="ruin",add="35db727f"},{q="Is the Uplands dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The Uplands serves as the primary stronghold of the Syndicate, harboring their heaviest concentration of fighters anywhere in the mountains. Wandering bandits, outlaws, and rogue nobles patrol the hills, fiercely guarding their camps against any outsiders who intrude on their territory.",al={"is uplands dangerous","uplands danger","how dangerous is uplands"},it="danger",add="4211f63f"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can see how displaced nobles organized the Syndicate's bandit network into a lethal force.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see Alterac's fall in these hills. Once they fed a flourishing kingdom; now cutthroats and ruined ambitions hold them."},kw={"alterac","baron vardus","breadbasket","dandred's fold","mountains","syndicate","uplands"},rel={"zone:alterac","topic:syndicate","topic:alterac-kingdom","subzone:dandred-s-fold"},src={"Uplands"}}
E["zone:alterac"] = {t="zone",n="Alterac Mountains",z="alterac",s="Across the Alterac Mountains, ruined peaks shelter ogres, outlaws, and the remnants of arcane power. Once home to the human kingdom of Alterac and Dalaran’s scholarly magocracy, these highlands draw travelers from nearby foothill settlements and the rebuilding city.",h="Across the Alterac Mountains, ruined peaks shelter ogres, outlaws, and the remnants of arcane power.",sec={{t="The Fallen Kingdom",b="During the Second War, Alterac stood among humanity’s Seven Kingdoms. King Aiden Perenolde betrayed the Alliance of Lordaeron and joined the Old Horde, hoping to save his realm. His treachery was uncovered and crushed, and the kingdom broke into disputed borderlands. After Alterac dissolved, the Third War brought fresh horrors. Its grand stone capital now lies in ruins.\n\nThe Crushridge ogres occupy the Ruins of Alterac under Mug'thol’s leadership. Alterac’s surviving human nobles formed the Syndicate, a vicious band of criminals. They fight by force to reclaim their lost estates.",sp=0},{t="The Rebuilding City",b="On the mountains’ western edge, Dalaran’s surviving magi rebuild beside lordamere lake. The demon lord Archimonde devastated the great city-state during the Third War. Its magi raised a massive, opaque violet dome over the ruins, but the shield has since been removed. The kirin tor now rebuild their sanctum in the open. Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver can be found inside the Violet Citadel.",sp=0},{t="Frontiers of Conflict",b="Southshore and Tarren Mill are staging grounds for journeys into the peaks. Yeti, mountain lions, and Syndicate footpads roam here. Beneath the snow line, a greater conflict churns.\n\nDeep in the mountain passes, the dwarven Stormpike Guard and the reclusive Frostwolf clan of orcs contest Alterac Valley. They fight over ancient territorial and mining rights.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to the Kingdom of Alterac?",a="During the Second War, King Aiden Perenolde betrayed the Alliance to aid the Horde. Lordaeron and Stromgarde crushed the treason and occupied the land. When the Scourge swept through Lordaeron in the Third War, Alterac fell into anarchy, and Crushridge ogres took its ruined capital.",al={"why is alterac destroyed","what happened to perenolde","alterac kingdom lore"}},{q="Who are the Syndicate?",a="The Syndicate is an outlaw band formed from Alterac’s dispossessed nobility. Former Alteraci royals such as Lord Aliden Perenolde lead it. Cutthroats, highwaymen, and disgraced lords terrorize the surrounding lands and drive out rivals as they fight to reclaim their ancestral domains.",al={"who is the syndicate","why are there human bandits in alterac","syndicate lore"}},{q="What happened to Dalaran's glowing dome?",a="After Archimonde devastated Dalaran during the Third War, the surviving Kirin Tor raised a protective magical shield over the ruins. The shield has since been removed, and the city is rebuilding in the open. Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver can be found in the Violet Citadel.",al={"purple dome alterac","what is the violet bubble","dalaran shield"}},{q="Where can I find flight paths or safe inns in Alterac?",a="Southshore and Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills are the usual staging grounds for journeys into the snowy peaks. Dalaran on the western edge is open to Alliance travelers as the Kirin Tor rebuild it, though it has no flight master. The Horde is hated by the Kirin Tor and attacked on sight in the city.",al={"alterac flight path","alterac inn","alterac quest hub"}},{q="What is Alterac Valley?",a="Alterac Valley is an isolated, snowy vale contested by the dwarven Stormpike Guard and the Frostwolf clan of orcs. The Stormpikes came on an archaeological expedition, provoking an all-out territorial war with the Frostwolves. The Frostwolves had lived peacefully in the valley since their exile in the First War.",al={"av entrance","frostwolf vs stormpike","where is alterac valley"}},{q="What is Ravenholdt Manor?",a="Ravenholdt Manor lies hidden in an obscure mountain fold east of the main road. Lord Jorach Ravenholdt commands the secretive guildhall of the League of Assassins, a training ground and haven for skilled rogues from across Azeroth.",al={"where is ravenholdt","assassins manor alterac","thieves guild alterac"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can find Ravenholdt Manor hidden in Alterac’s eastern cliffs. Lord Jorach Ravenholdt watches over elite contracts, lockpicking drills, and the guild’s secrets.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can walk Dalaran’s rebuilding streets, where arcane currents linger and Kirin Tor mages work. The city remains the devastated heart of human spellcraft.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you face Crushridge ogres and Syndicate outlaws in the former kingdom.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can find the Frostwolf clan at home in the secluded mountains. Forsaken agents out of Tarren Mill confront ogres and Syndicate outlaws.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you can find Wintersbite in Alterac’s frozen crags, its only natural habitat. The herb is an essential component in potent cold-weather concoctions."},kw={"alterac","crushridge","dalaran","perenolde","ravenholdt","strahnbrad","syndicate","uplands"},rel={"subzone:ruins-of-alterac","subzone:strahnbrad","subzone:ravenholdt-manor","topic:alterac-kingdom","topic:syndicate","zone:hillsbrad","npc:lord-jorach-ravenholdt"},src={"Alterac Mountains (Classic)","Alterac Mountains"}}
